    "title": "Michigan State women's basketball wins third straight game by more than 30 points - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kara Adams ,\n25 minutes ago\nEAST LANSING, Mich. (WLNS) – The Michigan State women’s basketball team secured their third win of the season Wednesday night, defeating Youngstown State 96-52.\nFollowing Sunday’s win over Eastern Michigan, MSU head coach Robyn Fralick challenged her team to improve on the rebounding end. On Sunday, Eastern Michigan out-rebounded the Spartans 31-30. On Wednesday night, the Spartans out-rebounded Youngstown State 36-24.\n“Tonight, we did a better job of rebounding the misses. You rebound better when you take predictable shots. I thought we took very predictable shots and did a much better job of getting extra shots,” said Fralick.\nMichigan State also scored 32 points off turnovers and 24 points off the fast break.\n“The ability to turn turnovers into points, that’s advantage basketball. The ability to get defensive rebounds and push, anytime that you can create advantage basketball, that’s a good thing for us,” said Fralick.\nForty-eight of the Spartan’s 96 points also came off the bench.\n“It’s so useful, especially the way we play. We play so fast and so hard that you gotta be able to have subs come off the bench and keep that same level of play, so I think it’s very important that we have that depth,” said senior forward Grace VanSlooten.\nThe Spartans will look to keep this momentum going when they return to the court on Sunday, Nov. 16th, when they host Western Michigan. Tipoff is set for 2 P.M.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.",
